WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:07.420
Fabio Ognibeni always enjoys working with
wood -- particularly if it has a nice texture.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:11.390
"The wood is smooth and even.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:22.490
That's just the right kind for making musical
instruments."

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:30.419
But a major windstorm on October 29 knocked
down almost all of the trees here in Val di

00:00:30.419 --> 00:00:33.590
Fiemme.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:48.440
"The next day, I felt like a friend had died."

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:54.130
The high winds blew down trees across entire
mountainsides.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:01:00.620
"It sounded like gunshots, or small explosions.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:06.990
When the wind knocks down an entire tree,
it makes an awful lot of noise.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:18.250
It's like the sound of a million branches
breaking."

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:23.590
Fabio has been coming to this area for 13
years to find just the right kind of wood.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:28.590
For centuries, the forest has provided wood
for violins, guitars, and pianos.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.120
The wood gives the instruments an excellent
sound and resonance.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:36.520
But now, Fabio is trying to save what he can.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:42.390
"This trunk has a good diameter, and a good
texture.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:47.310
But this crack right here shows that the tree
split when it was knocked over -- so I can't

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:52.130
use it."

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.670
Fabio wants to save as much wood as he can
before it's ruined by bark-beetles and other

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.570
pests.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:04.490
"I love this kind of work, and I love these
trees.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:11.640
This is my passion."

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:15.780
The wood is processed at Fabio's small factory
down in the valley.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.750
This is where mountain spruce is converted
into tone-wood and resonance-wood.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:30.340
Fabio's customers include a number of major
companies that produce musical instruments.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:34.180
This finely cut tone-wood will be used to
make violins.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:41.150
It's been sorted by age and quality.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:50.580
More than 300 years ago, Antonio Stradivari
crafted his violins from wood similar to this.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:55.170
But right now, Fabio is trying to recover
as much wood as he normally does in four years

00:02:55.170 --> 00:03:02.040
-- and it's going to cost a lot of money to
store it.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:07.800
So he's asked customers and private clients
to pay € 300 in advance per tree trunk -- to

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.200
cover storage costs.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:18.360
That's why he's choosing only the best wood
right now.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:25.849
"I've got to examine every trunk carefully
to determine which piece of wood would be

00:03:25.849 --> 00:03:36.489
best for each instrument -- and how many pieces
can I get out of a trunk."

00:03:36.489 --> 00:03:39.160
Only top-quality wood will be processed.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:43.519
Fabio keeps a close watch on all of the tree-trunks
– even in the sawmill.

00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:47.269
Here, the trunks are pre-cut along the grain.

00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:54.180
This wood will be used to make soundboards
for pianos.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:04:01.120
Sawmill Owner Franco Seber is sorry that so
many trees were lost in the windstorm.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:08.709
"It took those trees 120 years to grow to
maturity -- and then the storm ruined everything.

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:18.720
It's sad -- and now it'll take another 120
years for the forest to grow back."

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:22.720
Customers who appreciate Fabio's skill and
experience will support him during these tough

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.860
times.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:36.170
"Fabio has an extremely important job: he's
the only one who can find this kind of high-quality

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.290
wood.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.460
Violin makers like me couldn't do it.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.570
But we're all part of the process of creating
a musical instrument, so we have to trust

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:50.630
each other."

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:59.690
Every step of that process must be spot on,
as Fabio's tone-wood is made into a violin.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:06.030
"I'm happy when the client is pleased with
the instrument.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:11.750
The manufacturers and the musicians deserve
a lot of credit, too -- but people seem to

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:16.240
forget that it's my wood that makes the instrument."

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:19.340
Fabio Ognibeni's customers certainly haven't
forgotten.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:24.150
And for the time being, he'll continue to
salvage as much wood as he can from the Val

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:30.440
di Fiemme site -- so that he can keep providing
top-quality material for world-class musical

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:30.630
instruments.

